  "threshold_reasoning": "Threshold selection was performed strictly on the validation set across an expanded grid of [0.02, 0.90] with step 0.02 to avoid grid boundary artifacts. In job fraud screening, false negatives (missed scams) expose candidates to financial extortion and identity theft, while false positives trigger corporate registry (MCA/DPIIT) checks. Primary Balanced LR achieves optimal validation F1 at threshold 0.58 (Precision=85.45%, Recall=70.68%, F1=0.7737) and generalizes to Test F1=0.6569 (Precision=70.53%, Recall=61.47%). The Sigmoid-calibrated probability model achieves optimal validation F1 at threshold 0.38 (Precision=80.37%, Recall=64.66%, F1=0.7167) and exhibits near-perfect probability calibration (ECE=0.0045 / 0.45%, Brier score=0.0173)."
